\\quad b = 75, \\quad c = 24. \\]\n\nWe substitute \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) into the vertex formula:\n\\[ t = -\\frac{b}{2a} = -\\frac{75}{2(-25)} = -\\frac{75}{-50} = \\frac{75}{50} = \\frac{3}{2} = 1.5. \\]\n\nTherefore, the time at which the height of the ball is at its maximum is \\(\\boxed{1.5}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{1.5}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:188"}
